ElastiQP is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. 
It builds on four projects:

  * qpax (https://github.com/qpax-solver/qpax), Apache-2.0 --
    the elastic QP formulation and the kappa-relaxed smoothed-gradient
    technique. Portions of this work are derived from qpax.
  * ProxQP / proxsuite (https://github.com/Simple-Robotics/proxsuite),
    BSD 2-Clause License -- the primal-dual augmented Lagrangian algorithm
    that the PDAL backend (elastiqp/pdal.hpp) reimplements for the
    elastic form. proxsuite's copyright notice and license are reproduced
    at the end of this file, and apply to the portions derived from it.
  * PIQP (https://github.com/PREDICT-EPFL/piqp), BSD 2-Clause License --
    the proximal interior-point algorithm that the IPM backend
    (elastiqp/ipm.hpp) reimplements for the elastic form. PIQP's
    copyright notice and license are reproduced at the end of this file,
    and apply to the portions derived from it.
  * DAQP (https://github.com/darnstrom/daqp), MIT License -- the dual
    active-set algorithm (recursive LDL' working-set updates, proximal-point
    outer loop, cycle guard) that the active-set backend
    (elastiqp/das.hpp) reimplements for the elastic form. DAQP's
    copyright notice and license are reproduced at the end of this file,
    and apply to the portions derived from it.

The repository additionally vendors one set of third-party headers,
outside the installed ElastiQP headers:

  * third_party/xla_ffi -- the XLA FFI API headers (Copyright The OpenXLA
    Authors, Apache License 2.0; see the header of each file and
    third_party/xla_ffi/README.md).

PIQP's, proxsuite's and DAQP's own sources are not vendored; the benchmarks project
(benchmarks/, elastiqp_benchmarks) fetches their pinned release tarballs at
configure time for cross-solver tests and benchmarks.

